    "_siting": "Worlds since terrainGen 16 (world/townSiting.js): capitals, their first towns and the free villages stand where real towns grow. Every land hex gets a site score: terrain is the hex's own ground (and ringFertility x the mean of its neighbours'); water adds river (a river through it), riverNear (one beside it), confluence (two or more rivers join here), riverMouth (a river meets the sea here: harbour and river trade), lakeShore, coast, sheltered (the sea on only 1-3 sides: a bay, not a headland), bigRiver (a ford on a river fed by bigRiverFeed or more river hexes upstream), passFoot (beside a mountain pass, tile._pass, if the terrain marks any; a pass foot also cancels the mountain penalty), dry (no river, lake or sea within a hex); food counts wheat/fish/cattle/... resources within 2 hexes (each foodEach, at most foodMax); ore adds ore x the strongest ore field strength (tile.ores) within 2 hexes, so some towns are mining towns; desertInterior strikes a desert/dry hex with no river, lake or sea beside it, cold one in ice/snow/tundra; capitals on a land of fewer than islandMin hexes lose tinyIsland. capital: a capital weighs siteWeight x the score + its culture's favoured ground (cultureBonus, was 50) + distWeight x its distance to the capitals already placed + up to jitter (same sample count and spacing as before), then moves to the best scored open hex within refine hexes of the pick (no RNG). town: the kingdom's 1-2 first towns take the best scored open hexes of its land (score + up to jitter), spacing unchanged. village: a free village looks at up to samples open hexes (spacing unchanged) and takes the best (score + up to jitter). Worlds before 16 keep the old placement. founded: settlements founded in play in a world since 16 rank their sites by the same score read fresh (TownSiting.live; world/townSiting.js bestNear), within the founder's own rules. expand: a realm's new village (KingdomAI.tryExpand) (founded only when one could be on the hex it claimed, as before, so the pace of founding is unchanged) takes the best hex of its own land within radius of that hex (score - distWeight per hex, the spacing, crowding and donor rules unchanged) and is not founded when the best scores below minScore. pioneer: a realm's pioneers (Colonization.launchKingdomPioneers) add siteWeight x the score to their old reckoning (room, resources), then move to the best so-reckoned hex within refine of the pick; none go when the best scores below minScore. settler: a wandering party of settlers (WorldUnit.updateSettler) goes to the best hex within radius of the spot it drew (same rules: open, same land, more than 6 hexes from any town). bud: a village’s daughter party and the planner's suggested sites (VillageFounding.bestSites) rank by the survey score + weight x the site score; a site the player picks is never moved. dawn: a wandering clan (world/dawn.js) weighs its sites by siteScore + weight x the score, stays only where the score is at least minLive as well (a desperate clan still takes any ground), and a sea crossing adds seaWeight x the score. Worlds before 16 found as before.",
    "siting": {
        "terrain": { "grassland": 3, "plains": 3, "seasonal_forest": 2.2, "woodland": 1.8, "savanna": 2, "temperate_rainforest": 1.2, "hills": 1.5, "highlands": 1, "beach": 1.5, "island": 1.5, "boreal_forest": 0.6, "tropical_rainforest": 0.6, "desert": -1, "tundra": -1.5, "swamp": -3, "snow": -4, "ice": -5, "mountain": -3, "badlands": -2, "ash_plains": 3.5, "glacier": -6, "volcano": -6 },
        "ringFertility": 0.6,
        "river": 3.5,
        "riverNear": 2,
        "confluence": 3,
        "riverMouth": 4,
        "lakeShore": 3,
        "coast": 1.5,
        "sheltered": 1.5,
        "bigRiver": 1.5,
        "bigRiverFeed": 12,
        "passFoot": 3,
        "dry": -1.5,
        "foodIds": ["wheat", "fish", "cattle", "horses"],
        "foodEach": 0.75,
        "foodMax": 2.5,
        "ore": 1.5,
        "desertInterior": -4,
        "cold": -1,
        "islandMin": 40,
        "tinyIsland": -8,
        "capital": { "siteWeight": 8, "cultureBonus": 10, "distWeight": 0.35, "jitter": 12, "refine": 3 },
        "town": { "jitter": 3 },
        "village": { "samples": 14, "jitter": 3 },
        "founded": {
